Cell["\<\
Ising-type entanglers are two-qubit unitaries generated by Pauli product \
interactions. They are like time evolutions under an \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Ising\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Hamiltonian. Any \
nontrivial angle produces entanglement; at special angles they\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]re locally equivalent to familiar gates such as CNOT. They \
are also native gates to many types of quantum hardware.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9687531351929493`*^9, 3.968753191851902*^9}, {
  3.968753223104019*^9, 3.968753230833391*^9}, {3.971796963927723*^9, 
  3.9717969713531837`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cad95cb6-9a8f-4a40-a34f-\
fe5211fc0818"]
}, Open  ]],

